# The ring lets us easily select which symbol we want the gnomon's
# shadow to point at. This is important since the larger shadow of
# the giant gnomon will point to the corresponding toadstool, and
# when that toadstool is so selected, its white door opens. Since
# aligning the screw threads is the only useful application of the
# flipped world, this script revisits the arbor to flip us back and
# then ignores the arbor thereafter. It's less confusing that way.

d. d. s. sw. e. n. u. s. d. w. ne. n

nw
examine flytrap
e
examine tree
examine chasm
