# THE LUMP IS THE WHOLE PUZZLE, and here is where it silently goes
# wrong: with everything else in your arms, "take axe and lump"
# answers "The axe: Taken. The lump of metal: Your load is too
# heavy." -- and everything at the orbit site downstream of this
# line is doomed twenty turns before you find out (the statuette
# lesson, at orbital velocity). The lump is a magnet; the spade
# and walkie even tug toward it in your hands. Shed the ballast
# first -- this stash is where the endgame collects its kit
# anyway, and the shroud and bandage wait here safely.

drop spade
drop bandage
drop shroud
take axe and lump
u. u
turn ring to second symbol
d. d. nw. n
enter dish
wait
wait
s. sw
enter door

# Earth Orbit -- and the site the forums call impossible. It is
# not; the walkthroughs merely lost the load-bearing item. Read
# from this release's own ZIL source (I-ORBIT, events.zil): the
# site runs an eight-beat clock, and everything hangs on CARRYING
# THE MAGNETIC LUMP from the silo. Beat 4, it tugs in your arms;
# beat 5, PLOOP -- it leaps to the satellite's hull and anchors
# your soap bubble ("Where gnomon has gone before," grumbles the
# voice); beats 6-8 the satellite ferries you back toward the
# white door it is aimed at. At "The white door is very close
# now," break the bubble: "You're blown violently away from the
# satellite, straight towards the white door. The plutonium heart
# of the satellite erupts in a searing glare as you cross the
# threshold..." The break IS the exit -- one beat later the blast
# takes everything. Without the lump you drift past the satellite
# and choose between suffocation and incineration, which is the
# timeline every walkthrough transcribed. The skink dies en route:
# vacuum-side chores for the magpie's recipe.

take skink
kill it
wait
wait
wait
wait
break bubble with axe

